course: dictionary
lesson: 12664
title: Formal words: dissolution
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dissolution is a noun, a naming word for something that happens. It comes from the verb dissolve, which means to break up or melt into something else. Its meaning changes a little depending on the situation.
explain: In science lessons you may say «dissolving» when salt disappears into water. Dissolution is the more formal word for the same idea, and you will meet it in history, citizenship and official writing.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The dissolution of Parliament» comes before an election, so it means an official ending. «The dissolution of a partnership» is about two people or groups ending their work together.
fact: Dissolution is a noun, and it means the official ending or breaking up of something.
fact: «Dissolution» can mean the official ending of a group, organisation, parliament, marriage or agreement.
fact: In science, «dissolution» means a solid mixing into a liquid until you can no longer see it.
fact: «The Dissolution of the Monasteries» is a name from English history, when the king closed them.
fact: «Dissolution» is more formal than «breaking up» or «dissolving».
exercise: «The dissolution of Parliament meant that an election would soon be held.» What does dissolution mean here? | A long, happy meeting of MPs | A new law passed in a hurry | *The official ending of Parliament before an election | Parliament going on holiday
exercise: «The dissolution of the sugar in the tea took only seconds.» What is happening to the sugar? | It turns into a gas and floats away | *It mixes into the liquid until you can no longer see it | It freezes into a hard lump | It gets bigger and heavier
exercise: «After the dissolution of the club, the members went their separate ways.» Find and copy the word that tells you the club officially stopped. | ways | separate | members | *dissolution
test: «The dissolution of their partnership was sad, but both sides agreed.» What does dissolution mean here? | Two people sharing a tent | *The official ending of their working partnership | A happy wedding | A new shop opening
test: A teacher says, «The dissolution of the old bridge took years.» What does she mean? | A party held on the bridge | *The bridge slowly breaking up and falling apart | The bridge being built | The bridge being painted bright red
exam: «The dissolution of the old school was announced in May, and the pupils moved to a new building.» What does dissolution mean? | A big school party | *The official closing of the school | A school trip to a new town | A new school uniform
